:name: Neuron32
:description: Runs a NuASM binary on the co-simulated Neuron32 core.

$name?="Neuron32"

using sysbus

# Force Renode's built-in CoSimulationPlugin assembly to load before we
# dynamically compile CoSimulatedNeuron32.cs below. It is NOT loaded at
# Renode startup (confirmed via `python "System.AppDomain.CurrentDomain
# .GetAssemblies()"` — CoSimulationPlugin is absent until something
# actually references a `CoSimulated.*` type); the ad-hoc compiler used by
# `include @*.cs` only sees currently-loaded assemblies
# (AdHocCompiler.cs -> AssemblyHelper.GetAssembliesLocations() ->
# AppDomain.CurrentDomain.GetAssemblies()), so without this step compiling
# CoSimulatedNeuron32.cs fails with "type or namespace CoSimulatedCPU could
# not be found" even though the class and its base are both real and
# public.
#
# This warmup peripheral is created on its OWN throwaway machine and
# removed (`mach rem`) before the real machine exists — NOT added to
# $name. `start` below starts every machine in the emulation, and this
# peripheral is never given a SimulationFilePath, so if it were left in
# the real machine its own connection-setup timer would fire on `start`
# and crash with a null-pointer Marshal error (this is exactly what
# happened during development: don't "simplify" this back to a single
# machine without re-testing a real `start`).
mach create "neuron_plugin_warmup"
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "warmup: CoSimulated.CoSimulatedUART @ sysbus <0x70000000, +0x100>"
mach rem "neuron_plugin_warmup"

include @renode/CoSimulatedNeuron32.cs

mach create $name
using sysbus
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/platforms/neuron.repl

$cpuMacOS?=@renode/build/libVtop.dylib
$cpuLinux?=@renode/build/libVtop.so
$program?=@sim/testvectors/hello.bin

cpu SimulationFilePathMacOS $cpuMacOS
cpu SimulationFilePathLinux $cpuLinux

sysbus LoadBinary $program 0x0

# No `cpu PC 0x0` here on purpose — see renode/README.md and the note at
# the top of CoSimulatedNeuron32.cs. The RTL's own reset already sets
# PC=0, which is all this needs.

start
